      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "value": "@{5add6a46ab116f3eed7c4b0c|full_name}: True it would be hard to have a perfectly calibrated auto-system, but literally any tool that helps new creators find and fix issues faster instead of relying on the 24hr cycle would be helpful.  Ideas: Unity script you can use in Local Test to average drawcalls/cpu use/etc in graph mode. A network-based \"follow bot\" that mimics dev testers' systems and outputs a simple log/specs/fps. A script that just crunches your basic build file to check some basic settings (realtime lights/occlusion baked/#polys/#materials).",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
